# Full EA-3 v2 feature set. (It was cut to 'emmc' during Home Assistant bring-up;
# sgx came back once confirmed on the EA3, and switch + audio are RE-ENABLED here.)
#
# !!! SIZE: an x86_64 EA-3 kernel already fills ~7,037,952 of CEFDK's 7,417,856-byte
# bootlinux window; with sgx also on, switch+audio must not push it over (an
# oversized bzImage is TRUNCATED silently and does not boot). Status:
#   switch - now built =m (b53/dsa/tag), loaded by /etc/init.d/S39ea-switch, so
#            it no longer costs the window. SPI master stays =y.
#   audio  - still =y: SND_SOC=m would make the obj-y ASoC drivers fail the
#            vmlinux link (they call snd-soc-core exports), and making those
#            copied drivers obj-m is a separate change not done here. So audio
#            still spends its full size in the bzImage, alongside sgx.
# STILL NEEDS A CI BUILD to confirm the image fits + boots, and that S39ea-switch
# actually brings the switch up. `audio` also has never been built for x86_64
# (compile risk); its platform driver is probe-only (enable_pcm=0, reading TX
# reg 0x2004 hangs the SoC).
#
# Shared EA feature sets this board pulls in. One word per feature, space
# separated. Each lives in board/ea/common/features/<name>/, holding both its
# halves: defconfig (userspace) and linux.fragment (kernel).
#   wifi  - Atheros ath9k radio + wpa_supplicant/iw userspace
#   emmc  - sdhci-pci + ext4, persistent rootfs on mmcblk0p1
#   switch - BCM53125 managed switch over SPI (DSA/b53); gives lan1/lan2
#   sgx    - PowerVR SGX545 kernel driver (3D); gives /dev/dri/card0
#   audio  - CE5300 I2S + ADAU1451 codec, ALSA, AirPlay (shairport-sync)
#            and Spotify Connect (librespot)
emmc sgx switch audio
